            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air sealing beyond the 10% improvement mentioned above will result in more significant savings. This could be difficult to achieve unless performed during other renovation upgrades (walls, ceiling). </airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Upgrading the wall insulation can be quite expensive but result in significant energy savings. It is also a perfect time to perform air sealing and install new windows. Increasing the insulation by a minimum of R-20 will be eligible for a Good Energy Rebate. </mainWalls>
                <HeatingSystem>As this house uses electric baseboard heat I highly recommend installing a Cold Climate Heat Pump. They are affordable to install, as well as eligible for Good Energy rebates. Heat pumps will operate at 200% efficiency on average over traditional electric heat.  I can provide more information on brands and models for our climate if requested. </HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
